From e115818f501dbc5987bf228740b76f26491eca1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Upamanyu Sharma <sharma.upamanyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:58:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wal: take w.mu in Sync

WAL.Sync read w.locks (through tail()) without the WAL's mutex, while
ReleaseLockTo rewrites w.locks under it. The server calls them from two
goroutines (the raft loop's storage.Sync, the apply thread's
storage.Release), so they race. TestStorageSyncConcurrentWithRelease
reproduces it under go test -race; with Sync taking w.mu it passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 server/storage/sync_release_race_test.go | 93 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 server/storage/wal/wal.go                |  2 +
 2 files changed, 95 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 server/storage/sync_release_race_test.go

diff --git a/server/storage/sync_release_race_test.go b/server/storage/sync_release_race_test.go
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..0b3269dc0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/server/storage/sync_release_race_test.go
@@ -0,0 +1,93 @@
